answer_text:
Primary: read-more clicks per assigned post after 24h, comparing link placement to improve content engagement.
Reactions are plentiful but mix activity and overlap likes/comments;
likes are simple positive signals but shallow;
comments show discussion but may be spam or our own link comment;
read-more measures opening but not an outbound visit;
shares extend reach but can be viral or negative.
Sports/reviews and the junior-written posts have different patterns, so balance category and quality.
A day captures nearly all views.
Randomize to infer the link effect, report uncertainty at the post-assignment level, and choose one main metric before seeing results to avoid cherry-picking.

Choose shop1: its 1.8 is a higher performance score than 1.6, so it is faster.
The means already settle the question;
no other information is needed.

